Looking at the checkpoint requirements, I need to implement a minimal `mkdir` that:
1. Creates directories (single-level, no `-p`) with mode 0777 (umask applied by kernel)
2. Supports only `--` as option terminator
3. Handles byte-string paths, per-operand error continuation
4. Produces GNU 9.11-style diagnostics
5. Exits 0 only if all succeed, else 1

Key observations from the test suite:
- All 28 visible cases use `property:created` which checks exit_code==0 and targets exist as dirs
- The engine uses `std::fs::create_dir` equivalent (mkdir(2) with mode 0777, kernel applies umask)
